  "description": "Fuaran.Compute.GeometricAlgebra — a pinned conformal geometric algebra, Cl(4,1): the multivector over the null basis n0 e1 e2 e3 n∞, thirty-two coefficients in one published blade order, and the products every operation is written in — geometric, outer, left contraction and scalar, each one fold from +0.0 over one table of 1,024 signed terms in one order, a rounded product and then a rounded sum — with the reverse, the grade involution, grade projection, and the dual and its inverse as copies and exact negation; and the objects of Euclidean space as blades: the point, the point pair, the line, the circle, the plane and the sphere, each built from its parameters and through its points, with the join, the meet, read-back, the kind of a blade, and incidence as a value and as a test under a threshold the caller passes on every call; and the versors: the rotor, the translator, the motor, the dilator and the reflection, each built from its parameters, applied by the sandwich with its reverse, composed by one product, with the exponential, the logarithm and interpolation of a rotor and of a motor, an explicit normalisation, and a similarity as sixteen doubles both ways. No fused multiply-add and no host mathematics call but the correctly rounded root on any host; the sine, the cosine and the arc tangent are the pinned ones of Fuaran.Compute.Elementary, the one package it references beside FSharp.Core. So every answer is the same bits on .NET, under Fable and in every host that transcribes it. Fable-clean.",
